-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/08476006-9a68-50ec-8ca9-0b7964514a8d
-- title:
--   Semistable normal model over the henselian descent base A₀
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ denotes `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`; a *place* of an extension $K \subseteq F$ is a valuation subring of $F$ containing the image of $K$, different from $F$ and a principal ideal ring; for a point $x$ of a scheme, $x \rightsquigarrow y$ means that $x$ specialises to $y$, so that '$x$ is closed' reads '$\forall y,\ x \rightsquigarrow y \to y = x$' and '$x$ is not closed' reads '$\exists z,\ x \rightsquigarrow z \wedge z \neq x$'. For an integral scheme $X$ with a ring isomorphism $\varphi : F \simeq X.\mathrm{functionField}$, `SemistableModel.localRing X φ x` is the subring of $F$ obtained by transporting along $\varphi^{-1}$ the image of the stalk at $x$ in the function field, and `SemistableModel.baseToFunctionField` is the canonical ring map from the base ring to the function field, through global sections of $X$ and the germ at the generic point.
--
--   **Data.** A prime $q$ with $5 \le q$, a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$, and a valuation subring $A \subseteq \bar{\mathbb Q}$ with $q$ a non-unit of $A$ (`A.LiesOverPrime q`). A finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` — the intermediate field of the Laurent series field over the residue field of $A$ generated by `jqModC` and `jqNModC … M'` — over that residue field, required by `hW` to consist exactly of the elements of `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`, i.e. of the places $w$ that are rational (the constants surject onto the residue field of $w$), satisfy `IsAffineGeomPlace`, and whose value `w.evalAt (jGeomGen …)` lies in `ssJSet q`. A hypothesis `hle` that `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` (the $\bar{\mathbb Q}$-subfield of `LaurentSeries (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)` generated by the coefficientwise images of `modularFunctionFieldFull M'`) is contained in `fieldBar q M'` = `xHFunctionFieldBar (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')`, the analogous base change of the function field of $X_H$ of level $q^2M'$ for the subgroup `levelH q M'`, the kernel of the unit reduction map supplied by `dvd_sq_mul q M'`.
--
--   A constant-reduction datum $R_0$ (`ConstantReduction`) for $A$ on `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` with values in `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'`: a valuation subring `R₀.integers`, a surjective residue homomorphism onto the target field whose kernel is the maximal ideal of that subring, which on constants induces the residue map of $A$ and whose membership condition on constants is exactly membership in $A$, together with a place map preserving degrees, the scaling clause `exists_smul_mem` and the divisor-pushforward clause `mapDomain_placeMap`. The hypothesis `hR₀` states that every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` belongs to `R₀.integers`, and that its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over the residue field of $A$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$.
--
--   An element $\pi \in \bar{\mathbb Q}$ with $\pi^{q^2-1} = q$ and $\pi \in A$, and an element $\zeta$ of `Idx q`, the set of primitive $q$-th roots of unity in $\bar{\mathbb Q}$.
--
--   **The two families of valuation subrings.** Families $O^{\mathrm{Ig}} : \mathbb P^1(\mathbb F_q) \to$ valuation subrings of `fieldBar q M'` (indexed by [`CuspidalType.ProjLine q`](def/CuspidalType_IsCuspidalOfType.html#L21), the projectivisation of $(\mathbb Z/q)^2$) and $O^{\mathrm{SS}} : W \to$ valuation subrings of `fieldBar q M'`, subject to:
--
--   - `hIg_inf`: $f$ lies in $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell_\infty)$, where $\ell_\infty =$ `lineInfty q` $= [1:0]$, if and only if there are Laurent series $x, y$ with coefficients in $A$ such that the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ is nonzero and $f \cdot \bar y = \bar x$ in `LaurentSeries (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)`, the bars denoting pushforward of coefficients along $A \hookrightarrow \bar{\mathbb Q}$;
--
--   - `hIg`: for each $\ell$ there is $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ whose reduction `redQ q γ` carries $\ell_\infty$ to $\ell$ and with $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ the preimage of $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell_\infty)$ under the $\bar{\mathbb Q}$-algebra automorphism `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` of `fieldBar q M'`;
--
--   - `hIg_inj`: $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}$ is injective;
--
--   - `hIg_perm`: for every $\zeta'$ in `Idx q` and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ there is a permutation $\sigma$ of $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb F_q)$ with $(O^{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell))$ pulled back along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` equal to $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}(\sigma \ell)$ for all $\ell$;
--
--   - `hSS_A`: for every $s \in W$ and $x \in \bar{\mathbb Q}$, the image of $x$ lies in $O^{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ if and only if $x \in A$;
--
--   - `hSS_over`: for every $s \in W$ and every $f \in$ `R₀.integers` such that $f$ has non-negative order at every place of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ at which the element $\hat\jmath :=$ `coeffEmb (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) jq` of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` has non-negative order, and such that the $R_0$-residue of $f$ lies in the valuation subring of the place $s$: the image of $f$ in `fieldBar q M'` under the inclusion given by `hle` lies in $O^{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$, and for every $a \in A$ whose residue equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the $R_0$-residue of $f$, the difference of that image and the image of $a$ lies in $O^{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ and in the maximal ideal of $O^{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$;
--
--   - `hSS_fix`: each $O^{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ is invariant under pullback along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` for every $\zeta'$ and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$;
--
--   - `hSS_tr`: for each $s \in W$ there is $t \in O^{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ such that for every $a \in A$ the difference $t - a$ lies in $O^{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ and is a unit there.
--
--   **The descent base.** A subfield $K_0 \subseteq \bar{\mathbb Q}$ with $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ algebraic over $K_0$ and $\pi \in K_0$; a henselian discrete valuation ring $A_0$ (a commutative domain, discrete valuation ring, henselian local); an injective local ring homomorphism $\iota : A_0 \to A$ such that the range of $a \mapsto \iota(a)$, viewed inside $\bar{\mathbb Q}$, is exactly $A \cap K_0$ (`hιK₀`), and such that the composite of $\iota$ with the residue map of $A$ is surjective (`hres`); a generator $\varpi_0$ of the maximal ideal of $A_0$ (`hϖ₀`) with $\iota(\varpi_0) = \pi$ in $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ (`hϖ₀π`).
--
--   **Conclusion.** There exist a scheme $X_0$ in universe $0$, a morphism $p : X_0 \to \operatorname{Spec} A_0$, witnesses that $X_0$ is integral and that $p$ is proper, flat and locally of finite presentation, a subfield $F_0$ of `fieldBar q M'` with `fieldBar q M'` algebraic over $F_0$, and a ring isomorphism $\varphi_0 : F_0 \simeq X_0.\mathrm{functionField}$, such that all of the following hold.
--
--   1. $F_0$ consists precisely of those $f \in$ `fieldBar q M'` all of whose Laurent coefficients (at every integer index) lie in $K_0$.
--
--   2. For every $a : A_0$ for which the image of $\iota(a)$ in `fieldBar q M'` lies in $F_0$, $\varphi_0$ sends that element of $F_0$ to `SemistableModel.baseToFunctionField p a`.
--
--   3. Every stalk of $X_0$ is integrally closed.
--
--   4. The map $a \mapsto p^{\sharp}_{\top}(a)$ from $A_0$ to the global sections of $X_0$, through the inverse of `Scheme.ΓSpecIso`, is bijective.
--
--   5. Every point $y$ of $X_0$ lying over the generic point of $\operatorname{Spec} A_0$ (i.e. with $p(y)$ the zero ideal) lies in the smooth locus of $p$.
--
--   6. Relative dimension one on the special fibre: if $\eta$ lies over the closed point of $A_0$ and is not closed, and $\eta \rightsquigarrow y$ with $y \neq \eta$, then $y$ is closed.
--
--   7. A dichotomy for $\hat\jmath$: given that the image in `fieldBar q M'` of the element `coeffEmb (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) jq` of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, under the inclusion given by `hle`, lies in $F_0$, then for every closed point $x_0$ of $X_0$ lying over the closed point of $A_0$, either that element of $F_0$ or its inverse lies in `SemistableModel.localRing X₀ φ₀ x₀`.
--
--   8. Node structure: for every $x_0$ lying over the closed point of $A_0$ and not in the smooth locus of $p$, the stalk at $x_0$ is a Noetherian ring, and there exist $w : \mathbb N$ with $1 \le w$ and $w$ a unit in $A_0$, and a ring isomorphism
--   $$e : \widehat{\mathcal O_{X_0,x_0}} \;\simeq\; \widehat{A_0}[[u_0,u_1]] / (u_0u_1 - \varpi_0^{\,w}),$$
--   where the left side is the adic completion of the stalk with respect to its maximal ideal, the right side is `MvPowerSeries (Fin 2)` over the adic completion of $A_0$ at its maximal ideal modulo the ideal generated by $X_0X_1 - C(\varpi_0^w)$, and $e$ carries, for each $a : A_0$, the image of $a$ obtained from global sections, the germ at $x_0$ and the completion map, to the class of the constant power series $C(a)$.
--
--   9. The component–node dictionary: there exist injective maps
--   $$\mathrm{gen} : \mathbb P^1(\mathbb F_q) \sqcup W \to X_0, \qquad \mathrm{nd} : \mathbb P^1(\mathbb F_q) \times W \to X_0$$
--   such that:
--    - for every $\ell$ and $f \in F_0$: $f \in$ `SemistableModel.localRing X₀ φ₀ (gen (Sum.inl ℓ))` if and only if $f \in O^{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$;
--    - for every $s \in W$ and $f \in F_0$: $f \in$ `SemistableModel.localRing X₀ φ₀ (gen (Sum.inr s))` if and only if $f \in O^{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$;
--    - every $\mathrm{gen}(i)$ lies over the closed point of $A_0$;
--    - a point $x$ lying over the closed point of $A_0$ is in the range of $\mathrm{gen}$ if and only if it is not closed;
--    - every $\mathrm{nd}(e)$ is a closed point;
--    - for $e = (\ell, s)$ and $i$ in $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb F_q) \sqcup W$: $\mathrm{gen}(i) \rightsquigarrow \mathrm{nd}(e)$ if and only if $i = \mathrm{inl}\,\ell$ or $i = \mathrm{inr}\,s$;
--    - no $\mathrm{nd}(e)$ lies in the smooth locus of $p$;
--    - every point of $X_0$ different from all $\mathrm{nd}(e)$ lies in the smooth locus of $p$;
--    - every closed point $x$ lying over the closed point of $A_0$ and different from all $\mathrm{nd}(e)$ satisfies $\mathrm{gen}(i) \rightsquigarrow x$ for exactly one index $i$.
--
--   This is the existence of the normal, proper, flat model with Stein property over the henselian discrete valuation ring $A_0$ of the full level-$q$ modular curve (level $q^2M'$ with the subgroup `levelH q M'`), before base change to the valuation ring $A$ of $\bar{\mathbb Q}$: its special fibre is described by the Igusa components indexed by $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb F_q)$ and the supersingular components indexed by the supersingular places $W$, meeting in ordinary double points of width prime to $q$, the local rings being read off on the subfield $F_0$ of functions with $q$-expansion coefficients in $K_0$. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_semistableScheme_descent_of_valuationSubrings_and_smoothLocus_iff_of_isUnit_width_jDich`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_semistableScheme_descent_of_valuationSubrings_and_smoothLocus_iff_of_isUnit_width_jDich), the descent step of the semistable-reduction analysis at $q$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_exists_semistableScheme_over_descentBase_of_valuationSubrings_of_eq_pi_relDimOne_jDich.lean

import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_FullLevelSemistableCovering
